[2] LEMMA C1-U (PROVED)  f(1^m) = ceil(m/2) + 2 for every m >= 0
    Proof: sum(1^m)=m, so the head is W+(1)=[1,1,1,0] when m even and W-(1)=[1,1,0,0] when
    m odd; hence the list is [1]^{m+2} u [0] (m even) or [1]^{m+1} u [0]^2 (m odd).
    residue([1]^{2p} u [0]^z) = p + z because each step deletes one 1 and zeroes one 1.
   f(1^m) = ceil(m/2)+2 verified for m = 0..40, and residue([1]^2p u [0]^z) = p+z
   => C1-M's bound ceil(k/2)+1 is ATTAINED at EVERY k >= 2 (k = m+2), as a THEOREM.
   CORRUPT: f(1^m) = ceil(m/2)+1 is violated                  hits=41       OK

